----------------------------------------------------------------------
Dependency: Glass
----------------------------------------------------------------------

GPI is built on and depends, at runtime, on Glass — a self-hosting verifiable
functional language with a from-scratch zk-STARK toolkit, which performs ALL of
the cryptographic proving in GPI. GPI does not reimplement any cryptography; it
generates Glass programs and executes them with the Glass engine.

  Glass — https://github.com/EgorKhaklin/Glass
  Copyright 2026 Egor Khaklin
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, or the MIT License.

Glass is NOT bundled with GPI. It is resolved at runtime from the path given by
the GPI_GLASS_DIR environment variable (default: ~/Desktop/Glass). Only GPI's
local prover invokes Glass; the registry server is engine-free.

----------------------------------------------------------------------

The cryptography provided by Glass is EDUCATIONAL-GRADE — a working demonstration,
not production-hardened security. See Glass's docs/soundness.md. Every artifact
GPI produces is labeled `crypto-grade: educational`.
